1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,143
Coach: Reflection is more useful when it connects to something specific that happened.

2
00:00:05,143 --> 00:00:09,857
Coach: Instead of adding a broad claim about becoming a better person,

3
00:00:09,857 --> 00:00:15,857
Coach: identify what you would keep or change and why it follows from the experience.

4
00:00:15,857 --> 00:00:20,143
Coach: You do not need to claim a complete personal transformation.

5
00:00:20,493 --> 00:00:22,636
Coach: In the fictional guide case,

6
00:00:22,636 --> 00:00:27,350
Coach: the participant found different room names on the map and schedule.

7
00:00:27,350 --> 00:00:31,636
Coach: The coordinator confirmed that they referred to the same room

8
00:00:31,636 --> 00:00:34,636
Coach: and that its sign said Blue Room.

9
00:00:34,636 --> 00:00:37,636
Coach: The participant then changed the map label.

10
00:00:37,636 --> 00:00:41,064
Coach: Those actions have already happened within the story.

11
00:00:41,414 --> 00:00:43,128
Coach: The reflection points forward:

12
00:00:43,128 --> 00:00:48,700
Coach: next time, the participant would agree a shared list of room names earlier.

13
00:00:48,700 --> 00:00:53,843
Coach: That could make the naming choice explicit before separate parts are prepared.

14
00:00:53,843 --> 00:00:55,986
Coach: It remains a proposed change,

15
00:00:55,986 --> 00:01:00,700
Coach: not a system the team has already introduced or proved effective.

16
00:01:09,050 --> 00:01:11,193
Coach: In a later practice conversation,

17
00:01:11,193 --> 00:01:15,050
Coach: Maya asks what the participant would change next time.

18
00:01:15,050 --> 00:01:20,622
Coach: Focus on that question before deciding how much of the story to repeat.

19
00:01:20,622 --> 00:01:26,193
Coach: The listener already has the setting; the useful new detail is the reflection.

20
00:01:26,543 --> 00:01:29,543
Maya: What would you do differently next time?

21
00:01:29,893 --> 00:01:35,036
You: Next time, I would agree a shared list of room names earlier,

22
00:01:35,036 --> 00:01:38,036
You: before preparing separate parts of the guide.

23
00:01:38,386 --> 00:01:41,386
Coach: This answers the future-change question directly.

24
00:01:41,386 --> 00:01:46,958
Coach: It does not retell every action or turn a plan into an achievement.

25
00:01:46,958 --> 00:01:51,672
Coach: Saying what you would do locates the idea in the future.

26
00:01:51,672 --> 00:01:54,243
Coach: If the listener asks for more,

27
00:01:54,243 --> 00:01:57,672
Coach: let that particular question guide the next detail.

28
00:01:58,022 --> 00:02:01,879
Maya: Why does that change make sense in this experience?

29
00:02:02,229 --> 00:02:06,943
You: The map and schedule used different names for the same room.

30
00:02:06,943 --> 00:02:12,515
You: I would propose agreeing the names before preparing separate parts of the guide.

31
00:02:12,515 --> 00:02:15,943
You: We have not put that change into practice.

32
00:02:16,293 --> 00:02:20,579
Coach: This follow-up asks for the connection between the experience

33
00:02:20,579 --> 00:02:22,293
Coach: and the proposed change.

34
00:02:22,293 --> 00:02:27,865
Coach: The answer starts with the mismatch, then explains what would be done earlier.

35
00:02:27,865 --> 00:02:32,150
Coach: It does not need to repeat the whole guide story,

36
00:02:32,150 --> 00:02:36,436
Coach: or claim that the list has already prevented a problem.

37
00:02:36,786 --> 00:02:41,072
Coach: Be careful about the cause you add to a reflection.

38
00:02:41,072 --> 00:02:45,786
Coach: The two labels differed, but both referred to the same room.

39
00:02:45,786 --> 00:02:49,643
Coach: The case does not show that Maya was careless

40
00:02:49,643 --> 00:02:52,643
Coach: or that the team ignored an instruction.

41
00:02:52,643 --> 00:02:58,215
Coach: Do not turn an information mismatch into an unsupported judgement about a person.

42
00:02:58,565 --> 00:03:02,851
Coach: The proposed list might make the naming choice explicit earlier.

43
00:03:02,851 --> 00:03:05,851
Coach: That is a reason to consider it,

44
00:03:05,851 --> 00:03:09,279
Coach: not evidence that it will prevent every mismatch.

45
00:03:09,279 --> 00:03:13,137
Coach: No later event in this case tests the idea.

46
00:03:13,137 --> 00:03:17,851
Coach: You can explain a possible benefit while leaving its effectiveness unknown.

47
00:03:18,201 --> 00:03:23,344
Coach: Try the original question privately: what would you do differently next time?

48
00:03:23,344 --> 00:03:28,916
Coach: Use the fictional case, or reflect on a truthful experience of your own.

49
00:03:28,916 --> 00:03:31,916
Coach: Answer the question before expanding the story.

50
00:03:31,916 --> 00:03:36,630
Coach: Keep any future change separate from something you have already done.

51
00:03:48,980 --> 00:03:51,980
You: I would agree the room names earlier

52
00:03:51,980 --> 00:03:55,837
You: so that the separate parts have a common reference.

53
00:03:55,837 --> 00:04:02,694
You: I have not tried that change yet, so I cannot say how well it would work.

54
00:04:03,044 --> 00:04:07,758
Coach: A focused answer may be shorter than the story you prepared.

55
00:04:07,758 --> 00:04:12,044
Coach: Respond to the question asked, add the detail that helps,

56
00:04:12,044 --> 00:04:14,616
Coach: and stop before adding unsupported material.

57
00:04:14,616 --> 00:04:21,473
Coach: A clear limit can be part of an answer, rather than a gap that needs disguising.
